<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Decelean War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">413–<a href="/years/404-bce">404 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Ionian War · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Decelean War, also called the Ionian War, was the final phase of the Peloponnesian War, from 413 to 404 BCE. On the advice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcibiades">Alcibiades</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> fortified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decelea">Decelea</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> as a permanent base, cutting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> off from its countryside and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines, while the war shifted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> with Persian money funding the Spartan fleet. It ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysander">Lysander</a>'s victory at Aegospotami and the surrender of Athens.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/decelean-war.jpg" alt="Decelean War" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Translator was Kenmayer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pelop_war_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
